            <ArticleTitle>Arthritis caused by group B Streptococcus: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>805-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0b013e31826288bf</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Streptococcus agalactiae is not only a well-known cause of severe infections in the first 3 months of life but also an unusual organism to be isolated in case of septic arthritis, especially in children. We report a case of a monoarticular arthritis in a 6-month-old girl.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
